      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=0.$\n- **II.** The function has a maximum value at $x=\\pi.$\n- **III.** The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176047/assets/cosine.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. At $x=0$, the function has value $\\cos 0=1$.\n\n- Statement II is false. $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$.\n\n- Statement III is true. $\\cos(\\frac{3\\pi}{2})=0$.",
